# JupyterHub H100 Environment Reference

## 1. Hardware

| Resource | Value |
|----------|-------|
| GPU | **NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3** (single, `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0`) |
| Driver | 570.211.01 |
| CUDA | 12.8 |
| System RAM | ~100 GB (Kubernetes allocation) |
| CPU cores | 32 |
| Persistent storage | PVC at `/home/jovyan/work` (~877 GB, NFS-backed, survives pod restarts) |
| Overlay root FS | 431 GB (ephemeral, lost on restart) |
| Python | 3.13 via `conda base` (no separate venv needed) |
| User | `jovyan` (default JupyterHub user) |
| Pod hostname | `orchestraiq-jupyter-*` |

**H100 advantages over A100:** 2x VRAM (80GB vs 40GB), native bf16 support (same exponent range as fp32, no GradScaler needed), batch_size=128 (vs 64).

