## 5. Pre-extracted fMRI Features

Created by `make preextract SUBJECT=subj01`. Raw ROI-masked voxels (no z-score, no PCA).

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| File | `cache/preextracted/subject={subj}/fmri_features.npy` |
| Shape | `(~30000, ~15724)` for subj01 |
| dtype | float32 |
| Size | ~1.8 GB per subject |
| ROI mask | `nsdgeneral.nii.gz` |
| Used by | `PreextractedNSDDataset` in `train_unified.py` |

Training always prefers pre-extracted `.npy` over NIfTI loading.
The ablation launcher auto-runs `make preextract` if `.npy` is missing.

## 6. Model Architecture Summary

### Model types
| Type | Encoder | Decoder | Description |
|------|---------|---------|-------------|
| `deterministic` | MLP | DeterministicDecoder | Single L2-normalized 768-D output |
| `gaussian` | MLP | GaussianDecoder | (mu, logvar) output |
| `vmf` | MLP or ROI Transformer | VonMisesFisherDecoder | (mu, kappa) on unit hypersphere |
| `vmf_dcf` | ROI Transformer (required) | ROIDCFDecoder | Per-ROI vMF experts + spherical consensus fusion |

### MLP Encoder
- Hidden dims: `[8192, 4096, 2048]` (v4+)
- `use_residual: true` adds MindEye-style ResidualBlocks after each projection
- Activation: GELU, dropout: 0.25 (v9)

### ROI Transformer Encoder
- 17 ROI tokens: V1v, V1d, V2v, V2d, V3v, V3d, V3A, V3B, V4, FFA1, FFA2, PPA, EBA, OFA, OPA, RSC, nsdgeneral_other
- `d_model=768`, `nhead=12`, `num_layers=6` (v5+)
- ROI indices dynamically computed by `build_roi_index()` from NSD atlas files (YAML `roi_dims` are nominal only)
- Output: [CLS] token (768-D) or per-ROI tokens for DCF
- Multi-subject variant: `MultiSubjectROITransformer` with per-subject ROI projections + subject embeddings (v7+)
- Stochastic Depth: `drop_path_rate=0.15` (v9)

### Contrastive Projection Head (v9)
- MLP: 768 -> 2048 -> 768 with LayerNorm, GELU, Dropout
- Separates contrastive loss optimization from retrieval representation
- Only used during training; discarded at eval/inference

### Decoder output dim: 768 (must match CLIP embedding_dim)
- Kappa parameterization: `softplus` (v7+), with `kappa_reg lambda=0.1` (v9)

## 7. Experiment Configs

40+ YAML files in `configs/experiments/`, organized across 9 generations:

### v1-v3 (legacy): initial implementations, nsdId bug present
Preserved for reproducibility. Not to be used for new experiments.

### v4 (baselines): nsdId fix, per-session z-score, MixCo, SoftCLIP
- B-series (B0v4, B1v4): deterministic and Gaussian baselines, ~22% R@1
- N-series (N1v4-N4v4): vMF models, 30-36% R@1 (kappa collapse)

### v5-v6 (N-series only): kappa collapse fix, novel losses
- v5: tau=1.0, kappa_reg off, EMA, noise aug. N1: 39.9% R@1
- v6: Delta-SPCL, vMF-SoftCLIP, Slerp MixCo. N1: ~40%

### v7 (N-series only): softplus kappa, multi-subject, multi-layer CLIP
- Softplus kappa, fused CLIP targets, multi-subject ROI Transformer. N1: **49%** R@1

### v8 (N3/N4 only): hierarchical CLIP alignment, CKA loss
- N3v8: 50.3%, N4v8: **50.8%** R@1

### v9 (current, all N-series): anti-overfit + H100 optimization
| Config | Key Features |
|--------|-------------|
| `N1v9_vmf_nce.yaml` | MLP + proj head + R-Drop + CSLS + TTA, dropout=0.25 |
| `N2v9_roi_transformer.yaml` | Multi-subj ROI Trans + DropPath + proj head + CSLS |
| `N3v9_roi_dcf.yaml` | ROI-DCF + DropPath + proj head + R-Drop + CSLS + TTA |
| `N4v9_full_system.yaml` | N3 + SPCL + DUA-CFG (flagship) |

All v9: batch=128, bf16, grad_accum=8 (eff. batch 1024), 200 epochs, patience 30.

## 8. Data Split Convention (v3)

- `split_by_image: true` — train/val split by unique `nsdId`, not by trial (prevents data leakage from repeated images)
- `exclude_shared1000: true` — shared1000 images held out entirely for final benchmarking
- Train 90% / Val 10% of remaining unique images
- `seed: 42` for reproducible splits

## 9. Pipeline Execution Order

```
Step 1: Environment setup
  cp .env.jupyterhub .env
  # edit .env (set HF_TOKEN, verify paths)
  set -a && source .env && set +a
  pip install -e ".[train,diffusion]"

Step 2: Preflight
  make preflight

Step 3: NSD data download (aws s3 sync, ~3-8 hours)
  # betas, stimuli HDF5, metadata CSV, ROI masks for subj01/02/05/07

Step 4: Data preparation
  for subj in subj01 subj02 subj05 subj07; do
    make index SUBJECT=$subj           # -> index.parquet
    make preprocess SUBJECT=$subj      # -> scaler, reliability, PCA artifacts
  done
  make clip-cache                      # -> clip.parquet (768-D embeddings)
  make download-sd                     # -> SD 2.1 model (~33.8 GB)

Step 5: Pre-extract fMRI features
  for subj in subj01 subj02 subj05 subj07; do
    make preextract SUBJECT=$subj      # -> fmri_features.npy (~1.8 GB each)
  done

Step 6: Training ablation
  nohup make ablation SUBJECTS="subj01 subj02 subj05 subj07" GPU=0 > ablation.log 2>&1 &

Step 7: Aggregate results
  python3 scripts/evaluation/aggregate_ablation.py \
    --results-dir experimental_results \
    --subjects subj01 subj02 subj05 subj07
  # -> ablation_summary.csv, ablation_summary.tex, ablation_comparison.png

Step 8: Reconstruction (optional, per experiment)
  make full-pipeline SUBJECTS="subj01 subj02 subj05 subj07" GPU=0
  # or selectively with decode_diffusion.py
```

